---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Features | Blood Kings Monitoring" description="Explore detailed features of Blood Kings Monitoring: from remote agents, to SSL certificate tracking, and instant Discord or email notifications.">
  <section class="page-header section">
    <div class="container text-center">
      <span class="badge badge-accent">Detailed Specs</span>
      <h1>Every feature, as it is built today.</h1>
      <p class="section-subtitle">Discover a comprehensive monitoring toolset designed for sysadmins, devops engineers, and independent developers.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Deep Dive Features -->
  <section class="section bg-dim">
    <div class="container features-deep-grid">
      <!-- Feature 1 -->
      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <span class="feature-number">01</span>
          <h2>Lightweight Remote Agents</h2>
          <p>
            The agents are plain scripts (Bash, Python, PowerShell, and ash on OpenWrt) that need nothing beyond their interpreter and curl. Cron starts them, they send one report and exit.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li><strong>Short Install:</strong> Download, register with a token, add to cron - on Linux, OpenWrt, Windows and Docker.</li>
            <li><strong>Secure Communication:</strong> Agents establish outgoing connections and push telemetry data securely via HTTPS.</li>
            <li><strong>System Metrics out-of-the-box:</strong> Gathers real-time CPU utilization, RAM usage, storage loads, and network activity.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-visual-mock card">
          <div class="mock-terminal">
            <div class="terminal-header"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
            <div class="terminal-body" lang="cs">
              <p class="green-text">$ ./agent.sh --register YOUR_REGISTRATION_TOKEN https://bloodkings.eu/status/agent_api.php</p>
              <p>Registruji nového agenta na https://bloodkings.eu/status/agent_api.php...</p>
              <p>OK: Agent byl úspěšně zaregistrován a nastavení bylo uloženo do /opt/bk-agent/agent.cfg (AGENT_KEY=…)</p>
              <p class="green-text">$ ./agent.sh --verbose</p>
              <p>…</p>
              <p>OK: Statistiky úspěšně odeslány.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 2 -->
      <div class="feature-row reverse">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <span class="feature-number">02</span>
          <h2>Beautiful Public Status Pages</h2>
          <p>
            Give your users confidence. Build and share customizable status pages mapping service metrics on your custom domain.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li><strong>Isolated Caching:</strong> Status pages leverage cached aggregates, meaning traffic spikes won't load your main monitoring database.</li>
            <li><strong>Incident History:</strong> Record downtime reasons, timeline events, and planned maintenance cycles transparently.</li>
            <li><strong>Custom Branding:</strong> Embed your corporate logo, adjust color styling, and customize navigation bars.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fact-panel card">
          <p class="fact-panel-title">What the public status page carries</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Current state of the monitors you make public</li>
            <li>Incidents with their updates</li>
            <li>Planned maintenance windows</li>
            <li>E-mail subscribers (double opt-in)</li>
            <li>An SVG badge and an RSS feed</li>
            <li>Your logo, colour theme and navigation links</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="fact-panel-link" href="https://bloodkings.eu/app/public" rel="noopener">Open the live status page →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 3 -->
      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <span class="feature-number">03</span>
          <h2>Instant Notifications</h2>
          <p>
            Don't rely on users to tell you when a service goes down. Receive instant alerts on any failure event.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li><strong>Discord & Slack:</strong> Embedded rich alerts detailing target, code, and response latency.</li>
            <li><strong>Email (SMTP):</strong> Secure delivery of outage warnings straight to your inbox.</li>
            <li><strong>More channels:</strong> SMS (Twilio), WhatsApp (CallMeBot), Telegram, Pushover and PagerDuty, plus an escalation webhook for incidents nobody acknowledged.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fact-panel card">
          <p class="fact-panel-title">Alert channels in the code today</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>E-mail (SMTP or PHP mail)</li>
            <li>SMS through Twilio</li>
            <li>WhatsApp through CallMeBot</li>
            <li>Discord, Slack and Telegram</li>
            <li>Pushover and PagerDuty</li>
            <li>Escalation webhook for unacknowledged incidents</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Feature 4 -->
      <div class="feature-row reverse">
        <div class="feature-text">
          <span class="feature-number">04</span>
          <h2>Monitoring That Admits When It Fails</h2>
          <p>
            The worst outage is the one your monitoring sleeps through. When the collector dies, a dashboard full of
            last-known green tells you nothing is wrong - so we made silence impossible.
          </p>
          <ul class="feature-bullets">
            <li><strong>Heartbeat monitors:</strong> Backups and cron jobs report in on their own. Nothing to ping, nothing to miss.</li>
            <li><strong>External watchdog:</strong> A Cloudflare Worker checks the collector from outside the server and speaks up when it stops.</li>
            <li><strong>Never invented:</strong> Unmeasured values stay empty. A blank is honest; a fabricated zero is not.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="fact-panel card">
          <p class="fact-panel-title">How silence is caught</p>
          <ul class="fact-list">
            <li>Each heartbeat monitor expects a ping within its interval</li>
            <li>A Cloudflare Worker checks from outside that the collector still runs</li>
            <li>The dashboard marks stale data instead of showing it as current</li>
            <li>A value nobody measured stays empty, never a zero</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA Section -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container text-center cta-container">
      <h2>Ready to take complete control?</h2>
      <p>Try Blood Kings Monitoring today. Completely free and open-source.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/download/" class="btn btn-primary">Download & Install</a>
        <a href="/docs/" class="btn btn-secondary">Explore Documentation</a>
      </div>


    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 100%, var(--surface-1) 0%, transparent 60%);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  /* Feature Rows grid deep dive */
  .features-deep-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6rem;
  }

  .feature-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
    gap: 5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .feature-row.reverse {
    direction: rtl;
  }

  .feature-row.reverse > * {
    direction: ltr;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .feature-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .feature-number {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand-500);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }

  .feature-text h2 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .feature-bullets {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .feature-bullets li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .feature-bullets li::before {
    content: '✓';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--brand-500);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  /* Visual mockups */
  .feature-visual-mock {
    height: 300px;
    background: var(--surface-inset);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .mock-terminal {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }

  .terminal-header {
    display: flex;
    gap: 5px;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .terminal-header span {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-color: #3f3f46;
  }

  .terminal-body {
    color: var(--code-text);
    line-height: 1.5;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .green-text {
    color: var(--up);
  }

  /* Fact panels: plain lists of what the code does, in place of the drawn
     mock status page and mock alerts that used to stand here. */
  .fact-panel {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .fact-panel-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-low);
  }

  .fact-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .fact-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-mid);
  }

  .fact-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--brand-500);
  }

  .fact-panel-link {
    width: fit-content;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--brand-500);
  }

  /* CTA container styling */
  .cta-container {
    padding: 5rem 2rem;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, var(--surface-2) 0%, transparent 70%);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin: 4rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .cta-container h2 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .cta-container p {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.2rem;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* Responsive media rules */
  @media (max-width: 992px) {
    .feature-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }
    .feature-row.reverse {
      direction: ltr;
    }
    .feature-visual-mock {
      height: auto;
      min-height: 220px;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .page-header h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
